    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be the point of intersection of the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be the point of intersection of the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. The distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> from the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is",
